se,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Under **Rule 6c-11(d)**, an ETF must keep:\n\n**1. Authorized participant agreements**\n- All written agreements (or copies) between an AP and the ETF or its service providers allowing the AP to place creation or redemption orders.\n\n**2. Basket records, for each creation unit purchased or redeemed**\n- Names and quantities of basket positions exchanged.\n- Whether it was a **custom basket**, with a record that it complied with the ETF's custom-basket policies and procedures under Rule 6c-11(c)(3).\n- Any cash balancing amount.\n- The identity of the transacting AP.\n\n**Retention period**\n- At least **five years**, the **first two** in an **easily accessible place**.\n\nTo my knowledge, these requirements are unchanged since the rule's 2019 adoption. Check for recent SEC amendments before relying on this.","ttft_ms":3280,"type":"result","duration_ms":3299,"uuid":"e5341102-9b9d-46b8-a6ca-650d9849b459","ttft_stream_ms":1186,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1186,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
